  "rationale": "Every path to exfiltration is blocked by mfa_admin. Exfiltration needs admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup. Each of these needs a foothold gained by auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, and all three require stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc, which needs admin_dc, and dump_dbadmin_adfs, which needs admin_adfs. admin_dc needs foothold_dc, and admin_adfs needs foothold_adfs. These footholds are gained only through auth_dc and auth_adfs, which both require NOT mfa_admin. With mfa:admin deployed, both are blocked. So stolen_dbadmin is unreachable, and exfiltrated can never become true. The attacker can still get as far as reach_internal, footholds on the appserver and apiserver, and stolen_admin via kerberoast, but cannot go further."
